{
  "title": "Giant Cell Tumor of Tendon Sheath",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6092/giant-cell-tumor-of-tendon-sheath",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 20 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Giant Cell Tumor of Tendon Sheath, also known as pigmented villonodular tumor of the tendon sheath, is a benign nodular tumor that is found on the tendon sheath of the hands and feet",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with a firm, nodular mass that does not transilluminate with MRI studies showing decreased signal intensity on both T1-and T2-weighted MR imaging.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually marginal excision of the mass.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**second most common** soft-tissue tumor seen in the hand, following ganglion cyst",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "present in 3rd-5th decade of life",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "it is most common on palmar surface of **radial three digits near DIPJ**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "enlarging mass",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain, worse with activity (or wearing shoes, for foot lesions)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "firm, nodular mass that does not transilluminate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pressure-type bone erosion can be seen in up to 5% of patients on radiographs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6092/images/pressure%20bone%20erosion%20gctts.jpg",
                  "caption": "Giant cell tumor of tendon sheath showing pressure-type bone erosion"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultrasound",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "able to demonstrate relationship of lesion with adjacent tendon",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "homogeneously hypoechoic, although some heterogeneity may be seen in echo-texture in a minority of cases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most have some internal vascularity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "MRI may be helpful diagnostically",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "appearance of the focal form is generally decreased signal intensity on both T1-and T2-weighted MR imaging",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6092/images/gctts%20mri.jpg",
                  "caption": "Sagittal T1 MRI Image of GCTTS"
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6092/images/gctts%20mri2.jpg",
                  "caption": "Sagittal T2 MRI Image of GCTTS"
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6092/images/gctts%20mri3.jpg",
                  "caption": "Coronal T2 MRI Image of GCTTS"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Histology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Characterized by",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "proliferating histiocytes, moderately cellular (sheets of rounded or polygonal cells)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6092/images/gctts%20histo.jpg",
                  "caption": "Histology slide of GCTTS"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hemosiderin (brown color) may be present, but typically less than seen with PVNS",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "multinucleated giant cells are common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Ganglion cyst",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "cystic component",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pigmented villonodular synovitis (PVNS)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "histologically identical",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "involves larger joints",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Desmoid tumor",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "fibroma/fibrosarcoma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "glomangioma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6092/images/photo.jpg",
              "caption": "Intraoperative picture of a Giant Cell Tumor of Tendon Sheath"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "marginal excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "5-50% recurrence rate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "more common if tumor extends into joints and deep to the volar plate",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tendon involvement associated with high recurrence rate",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "local recurrence is usually treated with repeat excision",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "operative approach is dependant on location and extent of the tumor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "No reports of metastasis in literature",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
